<div class="grid">
{cards}
  {card title=$title, tone=$tone}
    <p class="stat">{$value}</p>
    <p class="muted">{$note}</p>
    <a slot="footer" href="?examples/cards">Details →</a>
  {/card}
{/cards}
</div>

<p class="muted small" style="margin-top: 18px">
  Open the developer tools: each card is <code>&lt;pad-card&gt;</code> with a <code>#shadow-root</code> PAD wrote. The page
  loads no script for it - the browser builds the root from the <code>&lt;template shadowrootmode&gt;</code>, and the
  styles inside it neither leak out nor let the page's in.
</p>
